WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.990
The question I get asked more than anything
lately is, how can you say that Revenge of

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.700
the Sith was a good movie?

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:15.230
But after that, and I have my reasons, the
next most asked question is, who do you trust

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.230
in the media?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:21.130
I'm finding this question harder and harder
to answer, which is yet another indication

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.510
of how screwed up our political and social
system is right now.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:30.599
At the same time, it's hard to know just how
screwy our world is, or whether it's just

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:35.690
the loudest and craziest voices get amplified
on social media.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.460
Maybe the American revolution actually was
a bit nuttier than the history books say,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.640
but we'll never know, as George Washington
didn't have the chance to live tweet it.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:51.640
Without trust, we really don't have the basic
underpinings for a free and pluralistic society.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.899
We have to trust our elected officials will
do the jobs they're sworn in to do and carry

00:00:56.899 --> 00:00:59.970
out the promises they said they would deliver
upon.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:05.289
We have to trust our media will keep the political
elite in check and not just suck up to the

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:12.740
powers that be, and we have to trust our institutions
are strong enough to withstand corrupt politicians

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:18.160
and totalitarian ideologies that would strip
us from the very freedoms our system was built

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.160
upon.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:25.500
Of course, trust, without doing the necessary
work to make sure it's based in logic and

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.010
reason, is just faith.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:33.280
Having faith our politicians will do the right
thing, or our media will hold the politicians

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:40.300
to account, or that our system will just function
as it should, is basically a recipe for disaster.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.490
Slowly but surely our freedoms will be chipped
away at because faith isn't what guarantees

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:50.640
our freedoms, it is the constitution that
does so.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.470
Trust is built over time by repeated evidence
that you can actually believe that when someone

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.420
says something it's what they mean.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:03.009
You don't believe it simply because they say
it, you believe it because of a track record

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:06.660
of a person consistently following through
on their word.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.290
This is the opposite of faith, which is built
on the idea of believing in something without

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:12.510
evidence.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:17.020
We usually talked about these existential
issues in the context of god and religion,

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:22.460
but I think it would serve us all well to
ask some important questions about these issues

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.010
right here and right now.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.960
So now let me kick that question back to you?

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.700
Who do you trust in the media?

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.760
I'm guessing it's a pretty short list, though
if you've some good names I'd love to hear

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.610
them in the comment section below.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.790
And let's go a step further, who do you trust
in politics?

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.380
If you're the biggest Trump supporter out
there, do you truly trust everything that

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.620
he says?

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:50.640
Or do you accept his untruths because you
believe in his wider agenda?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.990
Accepting a certain amount of untruth may
be the only legitimate way to view politics

00:02:54.990 --> 00:03:00.840
and politicians, but when you add distrust
of the media to distrust of politicians and

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:06.640
toss in a heavy dose of social media craziness,
we end up with this confused conversation

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.450
in which we can't even agree on basic facts.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:16.201
This spot, where nothing is really true and
what we feel overrides what is provable, is

00:03:16.201 --> 00:03:19.190
fertile ground for those on the extremes to
take root.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.460
So who do I trust?

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:25.290
Well there's a wide range of people from Sam
Harris to Ben Shapiro to Larry Elder and Eric

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.500
Weinstein.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:31.130
Trusting these people doesn't mean they're
infallible or I agree with everything they

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:36.380
say, but it does mean I see they have a commitment
to the truth and have consistently done their

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.459
best to put it out there.

00:03:38.459 --> 00:03:43.430
They don't have all the answers and either
do I, but we're doing our best to find some

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.430
truth in the sea of craziness.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:50.600
For those of us who genuinely want to figure
out how to combat the forces of who want to

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:57.050
burn down the system or give into authoritarian
tyranny our work is cut out for us.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:03.099
As for me, I trust that it'll work out because
I see more and more of you speaking out everyday.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:05.579
You might say that a little faith in yourself
goes a long way...

